Node rotation (manrotate): frees each instruction's entry direction, which is legal for every glyph except numeric literals (value depends on direction) and U (absolute side turn) — a conditional turn's arms are relative so -1/0/+1 keep their meaning and just point elsewhere. Node cells never move so nearest-pipe binding is untouched. Gate upgraded from (cell,direction) equality to a canonical BFS isomorphism, since rotation changes node keys by construction. 2 turns kept, avg 11,816 -> 11,762. Honest result: the relaxation bound said 15.5% of the pacing man's corridor was going to forced approach directions, but that bound ignored congestion — replanning from empty with directions unchanged is 2.1% WORSE, so this grid is space-limited, not direction-limited. Rotation is worth 0.46% here, not 11.8%.
